{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And YHWH saw.</b> These too are Moses' words at the end, and the angel is called by the honored name, in the manner of 'for My name is within him' (below, 23:21), which I shall explain there; likewise the angel who appeared to Gideon, where it is written, 'and YHWH said to him' (Judges 6:12). Or HaShem saw that he turned aside to see, and commanded the angel to call to him. Therefore the word Elohim and this name are not the essential name but a name of attribute, as I shall explain; it includes every holy being that is not a body, nor a force within a body, as written, 'therefore Elohim whose dwelling is not with flesh' (Daniel 2:11), which is the body. And here Elohim is the aforementioned angel."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved השם as HaShem in both occurrences per divine-name rules; the second instance could refer to 'this name' (i.e., YHWH), but the syntax groups 'אלהים וזה השם' together as parallel referents."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:12.158984560Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}